        "rephrase": {
          "az5": "Surveyed 14 heterogeneous source datasets, owning identity-spine datasets and setting metadata boundaries for downstream modelling, yielding 14 source datasets.",
          "p_gg1": "Merged 14 public omics source files into a graph of 1,399 cell lines and 16,385 genes (~2.8M edges), then applied Leiden community detection to identify 19 clusters with modularity 0.822.",
          "p_ql2": "Audited 859,494 training rows for completeness, structure and duplicates, identified 44,369 excess duplicate rows, hand-reviewed 181 flagged records, and built topic-grouped training folds using embedding-based clustering.",
          "p_ql1": "Fine-tuned QLoRA-fined Llama 3.1 8B on a 15 GB GPU, training 0.52% of parameters, which raised answer completion from 32% to 52% and exact-answer accuracy from 16.2% to 27.3% on 99 held-out NuminaMath problems."
        },
        "profile": "Builds the modelling a brief needs and reports its limits plainly: gradient boosting (XGBoost churn), LSTM time-series forecasting with time-ordered validation, text clustering (SBERT, K-Means, DBSCAN) and 11,459 per-gene models (train Pearson 0.807 vs test 0.545). Works with clients: scoped a loosely defined brief at 180 Degrees Consulting into a stakeholder demo (5-star rating) and contributed to the client's production MCP server, now in live use. Deploys on AWS and GCP (Lambda, Cloud Run) with CI/CD and MLflow experiment tracking. Builds deployable ML models: forecasting (an LSTM time-series service), propensity modelling (an XGBoost churn classifier with Bayesian tuning and SMOTE) and customer segmentation (k-means, HAC and DBSCAN). Owns data workflows end-to-end in Python and SQL, from merging structured, API and web-scraped data through feature creation, tuning, validation and deployment (Docker, GitHub Actions CI/CD, MLflow, AWS Lambda)."
      },
